### 4\. Network architectures and protocols

These describe how devices communicate rather than necessarily being physical transmission technologies.

* Peer-to-Peer (P2P)

* Ad hoc networking

* Mesh networking

* TCP/IP

* UDP/IP

* IPv6 Neighbor Discovery

* Multicast networking

* Broadcast networking

* MANET (Mobile Ad hoc Network)

* VANET (Vehicular Ad hoc Network)

* Delay-Tolerant Networking (DTN)

* Bluetooth Mesh

* Zigbee Mesh

### Important distinction

No Access Point does not necessarily mean no infrastructure.

For example:

* Wi-Fi Direct: no traditional AP.

* Bluetooth: no Wi-Fi AP.

* LoRa: can communicate directly between LoRa devices, while LoRaWAN commonly uses gateways.

* Mesh: can operate without a central AP, but may use relay nodes.

* Internet communication: can work without your own AP, but still relies on internet infrastructure.

For your networking and cybersecurity learning, I recommend studying Wi-Fi Direct, Bluetooth, Ad hoc networking, MANET, Mesh networking, TCP/IP and UDP/IP first.
